h antiretrovirals because it induces CYP3A4 less potently than 利福平. When combined with lopinavir/ritonavir (克力芝), 利福布汀 exposure increases, requiring a reduced dosing regimen (e.g., 150 mg three times weekly) and vigilant monitoring for adverse effects such as uveitis and neutropenia. This makes 利福布汀 a strategic choice in HIV/TB co-infected patients where rifamycin-based therapy is essential but strong enzyme induction must be avoided [Data: Relationships (30267, 9314, 9316, 9319, 55876); Entities (3893, 11562)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Serious adverse reactions are associated with 利福布汀 use\",\n            \"explanation\": \"利福布汀 is linked to several notable adverse effects, including 中心粒细胞减少症 (neutropenia), 眼色素层炎, and 葡萄膜炎. These reactions require active monitoring, especially when 利福布汀 is used in combination regimens with boosted protease inhibitors. Evidence indicates that increased exposure to 利福布汀 in such combinations heightens the risk of these toxicities, underscoring the need for regular blood counts and ophthalmologic assessments [Data: Relationships (9314, 9316, 9319); Entities (15288, 16613, 17278)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"贝达喹啉 introduces cardiac safety concerns in multidrug-resistant TB regimens\",\n            \"explanation\": \"贝达喹啉, used in treating 耐多药结核病, affects cardiac repolarization by prolonging the QT interval. When co-administered with fluoroquinolones—which also carry QT-prolongation risk—the cumulative effect must be carefully managed. Although observed QT intervals rarely exceed 450 ms in monitored patients, the potential for arrhythmias necessitates ECG surveillance. Additionally, 贝达喹啉’s concentration may be reduced by efavirenz (an NNRTI), complicating its use in HIV/TB co-infection [Data: Relationships (4384, 19760); Entities (8625, 1863)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"克力芝 interacts with multiple drug classes beyond antiretrovirals\",\n            \"explana